  "body": "Found in the second read of PR #3465 (head baa356d20). This is not a defect of that PR.\n\n## What happens\nThe fallback of #3444 in `crates/kernel/src/machining_mesh.rs` calls `solidcore_tess::mesh` for the whole body. That function takes no cancel token. Cancellation is checked before the call (line 303) and after it (line 311), but not during it. The margin retry can run the mesher two times.\n\nThe split rounds are bounded (`MAX_SPLIT_ROUNDS = 16`), so the call ends. But on a large model the user cannot stop it.\n\nOnly a model that the old code refused pays this cost.\n\n## Wanted\nOne of these:\n- a cancel token in the mesher API (a change in solidcore-tess; check upstream first), or\n- a time or triangle bound for the fallback, with a named refusal when the bound is reached.\n\nAdd a test that cancels during the fallback and gets a clean cancel, not a hang.\n\n## Also seen\nThe display planner caps face 12 of `testdata/models/hole_on_pocket_wall.step` at 3.3 mm sag (the row `off: area` in `crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement/rows.rs:214`). If the viewport uses that planner, the user sees the wrong wall on the screen. Check this and report it upstream if it is true.\n",
